{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cef5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a070ab-e5ec-77e1-8b81-6518e8a08211"},"sequence":1493,"recorded_at":1780531400002981,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1229eb00-c1b9-42f9-9a80-dbf339369c34","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.started","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"1229eb00-c1b9-42f9-9a80-dbf339369c34","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1229eb00-c1b9-42f9-9a80-dbf339369c34"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"84665f92-3971-4b2b-96f2-10c222a13d67"},"task_id":"84665f92-3971-4b2b-96f2-10c222a13d67","event":{"kind":"started","task_id":"84665f92-3971-4b2b-96f2-10c222a13d67","span_id":"00a4764f033f1c1f"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cef7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a070ab-e5ec-77e1-8b81-6518e8a08211"},"sequence":1494,"recorded_at":1780531400002983,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1229eb00-c1b9-42f9-9a80-dbf339369c34","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"1229eb00-c1b9-42f9-9a80-dbf339369c34","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1229eb00-c1b9-42f9-9a80-dbf339369c34"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"84665f92-3971-4b2b-96f2-10c222a13d67"},"task_id":"84665f92-3971-4b2b-96f2-10c222a13d67","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"84665f92-3971-4b2b-96f2-10c222a13d67","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-45-1\",\n  \"command\": \"tail -40 LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check LOGBOOK format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"### 2245 — Reaching a refusal clause is not pinning it\\n- ROOT CAUSE: Every fixture for a *shape* clause in `internal/localstore/projection.go` — the checks that refuse a path because it is not the kind of file it must be — was a directory at mode `0700` or a symlink at lstat permission `0777`. Both are refused by the `verifyOwnerFileInfo(info, 0o600)` call on the following line, so the shape clause was reached but never decided anything the suite could observe. Five clauses survived individual disablement; the blob-leaf pair survived being disabled *together*.\\n- FINDING: A derived refusal inventory can prove a site was reached. It cannot prove the site decided the outcome. Those are different facts, and positive-path-only coverage of a refusal looks identical to real coverage in both the inventory and the mutant count until the fixture is built so that every preceding check passes.\\n- FINDING: The isolating fixture for this whole family is one thing — a FIFO created at exactly mode `0600`. Not a symlink, owned by the effective user, already owner-only, so only the shape clause can refuse it. It had been written once, for the lock file, and not applied to any sibling.\\n- ANOMALY: The blob-leaf regularity clause bounds availability, not only safety. `os.Open` and SQLite block indefinitely on a FIFO with no writer, so removing the clause converts a refusal into an unbounded hang inside `OpenProjection`. A negative case that calls the entry point inline would hang the suite instead of reddening it; the case must assert a bounded return. Mutant `m11` reddens after 20.04s at that bound.\\n- DECISION: Where an isolating fixture exists, pin the clause rather than annotate it `projection-refusal-subsumed`. The shard-kind clause was provably subsumed by `verifyOwnerDirectory` and was still worth pinning with a 0600 FIFO shard, because subsumption is an argument and a fixture is evidence.\\n- DECISION: `unix.Flock` mutual exclusion was advertised in `README.md` and pinned by nothing — the 6-worker convergence test passes on SQLite's `busy_timeout` alone. flock arbitrates *open file descriptions*, so holding one in-process reproduces a second process exactly; no subprocess needed.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/localstore/projection_unix_test.go` (8 new cases, bounded-open helper, fixture-isolation assertion), `README.md`. No production source changed — every round-5 finding was an evidence defect, not a behaviour defect.\\n- STATUS: Resolved. Full sweep of both projection-owned sources: 34 mutants, 34 red, no survivors, including two forward controls on the inventory gate. TASK-260830-3amrl9 rev6, handed to review.\\n\\n### 2129 — Derived-completeness gate blind to its own refusal class\\n- ROOT CAUSE: `internal/localstore/projection_refusal_inventory_test.go` derived expected refusal sites from the production AST but matched only `*ast.Ident` calls named `projectionRefusal`. Six live clauses written as bare `fmt.Errorf(\\\"%w: ...\\\", ErrUnsafeOwnership)` or as delegated `verifyOwnerFileInfo`/`verifyOwnerDirectory` guards were invisible to the gate whose job was to notice them, and shipped unpinned while 20+ funnelled sites were enforced.\\n- FINDING: A completeness gate over a *pattern* must also police the pattern. Deriving the expected set is not enough if the extraction rule silently excludes a whole syntactic class.\\n- FIX: Second funnel `projectionOwnershipRefusal` (`internal/localstore/projection.go:117`) keeps the refusal decision at its call site while preserving the owner-only cause; every projection refusal rerouted through a funnel. Gate now derives two properties — funnel sites need an exercised negative path beneath `openProjection`, AND no projection-owned source may raise a refusal outside a funnel. Build-context filtering added so a platform-specific refusal is not demanded from a platform that cannot run it.\\n- ANOMALY: I reproduced the identical bug class inside the fix. The new unrouted check sat behind `typed.Fun.(*ast.Ident)`, and `fmt.Errorf` is a `*ast.SelectorExpr`, so the exact class stayed invisible in code written specifically to catch it. First run of mutant m41 exited 0. Reading the new gate would not have found this; only the behaviour-preserving mutant did.\\n- DECISION: Assume \\\"unreachable\\\" last, not first. One clause presumed unreachable — the non-regular branch of `ensureProjectionFileModes` — is drivable through the real production entry by replacing a sidecar with a FIFO in the post-rebuild hook. Only three clauses are genuine TOCTOU re-checks, each annotated with the earlier check that owns the reachable case.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/localstore/projection.go`, `projection_lock_unix.go`, `projection_refusal_inventory_test.go`, new `projection_unix_test.go`, `README.md`.\\n- STATUS: Resolved. 15 mutants, 13 red as required, 1 designed control green, 1 documented subsumed green. TASK-260830-3amrl9 rev5, handed to review.\\n\\n### 2113 — A gate must prove its own coverage; so must a mutation sweep\\n- ROOT CAUSE: `requireMemberSet` was a byte-identical duplicate of `requireExactMembers`. `TestConstraintEnumerationMatchesRequireExactMembers` scanned only the latter by name, so `WorkspaceMember.*`, every Session Event payload, `Observation Event`, and `ObservationCounts` carried zero per-member enumeration rows while the README claimed a complete inventory.\\n- FINDING: That blind spot is why a real defect reached review — `internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go` `validateTerminalV4Payload` validated `terminal_backend_id` with `requireString` only, so `CalculateObjectIdentity` attested `AX.TMUX`, `../../etc/passwd`, an embedded NUL and 5000 chars. SPEC.md:890 (§4.B) pins it to 1–128 ASCII bytes matching `[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:[.-][a-z0-9]+)*`.\\n- FIX: Duplicate deleted, all 5 call sites collapsed onto `requireExactMembers`. Grammar enforced by `requireTerminalBackendID`. `TestRequireExactMembersIsTheOnlyClosedMemberGate` now derives every function emitting a closed-member refusal and fails unless that set is exactly `{requireExactMembers}`; the scanned file set is derived from the package directory, not a hand-written list.\\n- ANOMALY: The mutation harness aborted mid-run on the zsh reserved variable `status`, after applying mutant 1 but before its restore. The next run took its baseline backup from that mutated tree, so all 12 mutants were behavioural no-ops against an already-red mask and every one reported KILLED for the wrong reason. Caught only because the full-repo run afterwards failed.\\n- FIX: Harness refuses to sweep unless the baseline is green, and reports `NOT-APPLIED` for any mutant that left the tree unchanged. Re-run: 12/12 killed, 0 survivors.\\n- DECISION: Session Event payload members are pinned by mechanical extraction from the pinned SPEC's four `Exact payload members` tables into `internal/canonicaljson/testdata/session-event-payload-members.md` (39 event types, 204 declarations) rather than hand-listed across 134 version×event shapes.\\n- FINDING: The first extractor split on `</code>,` and silently dropped members followed by a bare `(G2)` annotation, losing `clone.planned.projection_plan_id` and `clone.failed.materialization_id`. The new derivation test caught it; review had not. Parse one `<code>` span per declaration.\\n- NOTE: General property, applies to every derived gate — an inventory must assert that the set of constructs it scans is complete for the package, and a mutation sweep must assert its baseline is green. A gate that cannot fail when someone adds a second copy of a check is decoration, and a mutant that \\\"kills\\\" an already-red mask proves nothing.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/canonicaljson/`, `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json`, `README.md`\\n- STATUS: Resolved; TASK-260830-1tax26 handed to review as revision 2.\\n\\n### 2321 — A local copy of a shared gate needs a pin, not a comment; a registry that only counts itself cannot see new code\\n- ROOT CAUSE (B3): `provhost.decodeStrictObject` re-implemented strict decoding without the shared `canonicaljson` surrogate rule, and Go's `encoding/json` replaces a lone `\\\\ud800` escape with U+FFFD silently — so Section 1.6 wire bodies carrying lone surrogates were admitted. Same class as the sibling story's decoder gap.\\n- FIX: local `hasLoneSurrogateEscape` gate in `internal/provhost/surrogate.go` (local copy because `canonicaljson` is frozen across both unlanded stories), called first from `decodeStrictObject`; one `\\\\ud800` fixture per production entry plus `TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON`, a 13-vector pin driving both the local gate and `canonicaljson.Canonicalize` so the copies cannot drift.\\n- ANOMALY: the first gate version used `switch` and reddened `TestAllProductionSwitchesAreClassified` — the package census bans switches as membership-gate hiding spots. Rewritten with if/else, identical verdicts, green. A gate's own residue rules apply to the fix too.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (B4): `tracecheck` verifies registry -> code only, so ~3,700 lines of `internal/provider` + `internal/provhost` landed with the gate green under gap prose asserting \\\"no provider manifest is implemented anywhere\\\". The census enumerates what registered itself.\\n- FIX: 4 acceptance cases + 4 section bindings (7.1, 7.6, 7.7, 8), 4 gap rewrites (5.5, 7.2, 7.3, 7.5), re-pinned hash; report now bindings=53 unevidenced=45 clauses 17/428. Reverse scan (every `internal/*` package owned or explicitly excluded) recorded as open work, not implemented here.\\n- DECISION (A2/A3/A4, recorded in code): CheckIdentity duplication is deliberate (different error surface, shared package frozen); Provider Protocol 3.0.0 is a stated non-owner bound, not a defect; provider's cause-appending errors must be rebuilt, not quoted, at the future cmd/ax lift (`refuseCausalLeak`).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provhost/surrogate*.go`, `protocol.go`, refusal inventory (floor 162->164), `profile_test.go` (cross-plane set test), `identity.go`/`doc.go` bounds, `internal/provider/doc.go` composition contract, ownership registry + pin + report/golden/README figures.\\n- STATUS: Resolved. `go test ./...` and `-cover` green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, admit-all and narrowing mutants red as required. TASK-260830-32jeti round-4, handed to review.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 10236,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2559,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
